[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35a0d67f-2001-5b60-b42a-f979cd7b3038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{4x}(1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519074} {:answer/id #uuid "753c754d-a64b-5a86-bf3d-b11e9cb247e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519175} {:answer/id #uuid "762e2957-2bdc-5c9f-8c82-28884cca64d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({e}^{4x}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519177} {:answer/id #uuid "a25c36b2-66bd-5740-89f4-e95b59786f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2x}({e}^{2x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519258} {:answer/id #uuid "c60203e4-de60-549e-8d11-366f51f688e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{4x}(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "753c754d-a64b-5a86-bf3d-b11e9cb247e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519175} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac258ea5-31b3-5f32-97e0-aac682319621" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7c92bc5-8061-56c3-9e0d-1e01c4282d73" :question/math-academy-id "q-95511" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y={e}^{4x}-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{2x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{4x}-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{2x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{4x})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{2x}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x}-2(-\\frac{1}{|{e}^{2x}|\\sqrt{1+({e}^{2x})^{2}}})\\cdot ({e}^{2x})^{′} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x}+\\frac{2}{{e}^{2x}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}}\\cdot 2{e}^{2x} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}} \\\\  & =4({e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f62924-6dd5-52ac-bd28-479c20aca94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519045} {:answer/id #uuid "75fd5efd-a360-53f9-9006-6a6a1d8e159f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9{y}^{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519176} {:answer/id #uuid "849cc2b5-4f4e-50d8-9169-5a909d23bf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519201} {:answer/id #uuid "d03e8f09-0450-5bd4-8ebb-657acd93cbc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519331} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3bcf1a-3dc4-5e1f-8c31-d1add2e63f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849cc2b5-4f4e-50d8-9169-5a909d23bf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519201} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ea5fec5-a0af-570b-bb41-e2eb4069b829" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f873ff79-08e6-53a2-8403-85dc4a081919" :question/math-academy-id "q-143633" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{14}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{14}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{14}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{14}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{14}\\cdot [27-(-1)] \\\\  & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{14})}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{28}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519607 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e8af9d3-e625-57a2-9753-9a16f2c5bfd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{3y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519158} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c0f0ef-519d-5451-a179-30787df74d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519264} {:answer/id #uuid "bed11b29-67d4-5909-9036-4139a697822e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+y}{3y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519305} {:answer/id #uuid "d1fe2e08-4582-5e78-9887-77cb0f66a621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+y}{y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519335} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5bfc28-404f-5301-a9fb-f28a54d7b0fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+y}{y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e8af9d3-e625-57a2-9753-9a16f2c5bfd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{3y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519158} :answer-field/id #uuid "83d69883-60e5-51a8-8587-9ac2f3c97229" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fde66fe1-1f42-5587-ae07-4dc1d6de7d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-144943" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3y+1}{8}, & 0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{8})}{(\\frac{3y+1}{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{3y+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{3y+1}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ad4d22b-acab-5ed4-80d7-49438eaa6ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519948} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a9fe0e-461d-5c50-9b13-e2d874c7c501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17 \\sqrt{17}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519960} {:answer/id #uuid "ae7b8d36-7fec-572a-aff6-b1b470283083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{17 \\sqrt{17}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519963} {:answer/id #uuid "dede3d58-8509-5b02-a30e-5c2edec92aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{285}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519972} {:answer/id #uuid "e96d81fd-09d1-5c57-816e-ef56ea09fc90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{17 \\sqrt{17}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e96d81fd-09d1-5c57-816e-ef56ea09fc90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{17 \\sqrt{17}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519976} :answer-field/id #uuid "42a780e2-ad8c-5ca4-b690-f0fe637d9239" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "316743f9-ae6e-5a5c-90d0-c46ad39f440f" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c3f6e03956e6002db05950b10d9608be87dd45a4bb75b3822e1ab754981eb19d.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}2 x y^{6}\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=\\frac{1}{y}$ from $(1,1)$ to $(\\frac{1}{2},2),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=\\frac{1}{t}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,t⟩,\\,1\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $1\\le t\\le 2$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}})^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{t^{4}}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{1}{t^{4}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=2 x y^{6},$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2 \\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right) t^{6} \\\\  & =2 t^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2 x y^{6}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\left(2 t^{5}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{1}{t^{4}}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2 t^{3} \\sqrt{t^{4} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve this using the substitution $u=t^{4} + 1,$ $\\text{d}u=4 t^{3}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2 t^{3} \\sqrt{t^{4} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{2}^{17}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{17}\\frac{\\sqrt{u}}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\right]_{2}^{17} \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right]_{2}^{17} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(17\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(2\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{17 \\sqrt{17}}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{17 \\sqrt{17}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519933 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "502b4fef-e465-5b61-8882-5e374dab527e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519931} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa47a8c-d91a-57c1-a9f1-0922f42018fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519934} {:answer/id #uuid "68c61336-093f-55bd-aa10-7226bb03c3a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{10 \\sqrt{5}}{3} + 4 \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519941} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff5fdaa-596f-587d-a87a-1b719d485ce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10 \\sqrt{5}}{3} + 4 \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519956} {:answer/id #uuid "d906e193-9c9a-5192-b2b6-679b2f764aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68c61336-093f-55bd-aa10-7226bb03c3a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{10 \\sqrt{5}}{3} + 4 \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519941} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee9402cd-0a21-588e-9736-a8a0d09641c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5487c7b6-44fe-5e39-9226-bf0a43081f99" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}2 x^{6} e^{- 2 y}\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=e^{\\frac{y}{2}}$ from $(1,0)$ to $(\\sqrt{2},\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=e^{\\frac{t}{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨e^{\\frac{t}{2}},\\,t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $0\\le t\\le \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{\\frac{t}{2}})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{e^{\\frac{t}{2}}}{2}\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\frac{e^{\\frac{t}{2}}}{2})^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{e^{t}}{4}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{e^{t}}{4} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=2 x^{6} e^{- 2 y},$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2 \\left(e^{\\frac{t}{2}}\\right)^{6} e^{- 2 t} \\\\  & =2 e^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2 x^{6} e^{- 2 y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{e^{t}}{4} + 1}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\sqrt{e^{t} + 4} e^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve this using the substitution $u=e^{t} + 4,$ $\\text{d}u=e^{t}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\sqrt{e^{t} + 4} e^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =1{\\int }_{5}^{6}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot\\left(1\\right)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{6}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[1\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\right]_{5}^{6} \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{2 u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right]_{5}^{6} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{2 \\left(6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{2 \\left(5\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(4 \\sqrt{6}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{10 \\sqrt{5}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{10 \\sqrt{5}}{3} + 4 \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519936 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1462cb59-c704-506e-a83c-16cf44ae2975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519917} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4517a3-aa53-5919-9bed-4810f2d2c48a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519927} {:answer/id #uuid "4c732881-a009-564d-95a7-a2eeeff3e247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{125}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519928} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7575b3-0dca-5cc3-83db-5f2b03ab84a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{123}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519930} {:answer/id #uuid "528322e2-0164-531d-815c-501f2c5a4e7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{61}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "528322e2-0164-531d-815c-501f2c5a4e7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{61}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519932} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e62414b-49f9-5db8-a201-3192213542b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5b75b6c1-d336-52ca-ae2f-f314c60fb3a9" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}\\frac{6 x}{y}\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $y^2=6x$ from $(\\frac{7}{6},\\sqrt{7})$ to $(\\frac{8}{3},4).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve can be expressed in the form $x=x(y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\ny^2=6x\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y^{2}}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=\\frac{t^{2}}{6}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\frac{t^{2}}{6},\\,t⟩,\\,\\sqrt{7}\\le t\\le 4\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $\\sqrt{7}\\le t\\le 4$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t^{2}}{6})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{t}{3}\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\frac{t}{3})^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{t^{2}}{9}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{t^{2}}{9} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=\\frac{6 x}{y},$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{6 \\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{6}\\right)}{t} \\\\  & =t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{6 x}{y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{7}}^{4}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{7}}^{4}\\left(t\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{t^{2}}{9} + 1}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{7}}^{4}\\frac{t \\sqrt{t^{2} + 9}}{3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve this using the substitution $u=t^{2} + 9,$ $\\text{d}u=2 t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{7}}^{4}\\frac{t \\sqrt{t^{2} + 9}}{3}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{16}^{25}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{16}^{25}\\frac{\\sqrt{u}}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\right]_{16}^{25} \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{9}\\right]_{16}^{25} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(25\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{9}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(16\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{9}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{125}{9}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{64}{9}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{61}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b01bf31-2ee2-53d0-94d2-836a1979c75d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519915} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7f8963-5894-537f-beb8-fd372b21c68a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519923} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c1f173-d6f1-508b-9bb0-95bc71c51c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38 \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519961} {:answer/id #uuid "df9f311c-5c28-5284-b186-7d31aaae46f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519973} {:answer/id #uuid "f537f4b8-eb49-5ef0-9790-4395f8071591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df9f311c-5c28-5284-b186-7d31aaae46f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519973} :answer-field/id #uuid "6400f1c6-0b7b-5401-8a4b-73a82dadcf86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "757a5531-af3b-53d8-af0b-e619bd9a8745" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}2 y\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=2 y + 1$ from $(5,2)$ to $(7,3).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2 t + 1.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2 t + 1,\\,t⟩,\\,2\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $2\\le t\\le 3$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t + 1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=2 y,$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2 t \\\\  & =2 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2 y\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\left(2 t\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}2 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}2 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\left[\\sqrt{5} t^{2}\\right]_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =2 \\sqrt{5}\\left(\\frac{3^2}{2}-\\frac{2^2}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =2 \\sqrt{5}\\left(\\frac{9}{2}-2\\right) \\\\  & =5 \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519947 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39dca523-9171-5e40-833c-978d9ad71849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519922} {:answer/id #uuid "473858c3-157d-5055-9739-f0d6b85e7989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519925} {:answer/id #uuid "754a7457-a3e8-51f7-b689-9b4291afc217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519943} {:answer/id #uuid "9aa6f2cf-f8b0-51f7-9093-58c3d7bf3ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519953} {:answer/id #uuid "fe15649c-aa4e-5adc-af44-f12a4b3fb802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe15649c-aa4e-5adc-af44-f12a4b3fb802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519982} :answer-field/id #uuid "86cb8063-be0e-59e9-b0ab-6ae36122c5ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a06b7a8-a31a-5d91-a4c2-27f8e724e7b7" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}2 y\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=2 y + 1$ from $(5,2)$ to $(11,5).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2 t + 1.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2 t + 1,\\,t⟩,\\,2\\le t\\le 5\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $2\\le t\\le 5$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t + 1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=2 y,$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2 t \\\\  & =2 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2 y\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\left(2 t\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}2 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}2 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\left[\\sqrt{5} t^{2}\\right]_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =2 \\sqrt{5}\\left(\\frac{5^2}{2}-\\frac{2^2}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =2 \\sqrt{5}\\left(\\frac{25}{2}-2\\right) \\\\  & =21 \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "498a3dd0-f17b-5f70-8b03-fc510f9aad6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{152 \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519926} {:answer/id #uuid "97f57c54-8701-5d8a-a5ed-fd3c0f65306b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519951} {:answer/id #uuid "af54eed5-bbc0-5fe0-84c5-eb933f76c6a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519964} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ae83d0-87f4-5859-85f3-d0abf6c9594d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519968} {:answer/id #uuid "ff9120ba-23f5-5da5-845b-c9f43ed0780a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff9120ba-23f5-5da5-845b-c9f43ed0780a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519983} :answer-field/id #uuid "a078cda7-6548-5368-8ce0-29f35e1abda9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c77817c-c092-573a-a129-dda1b7dbaf00" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}8 y\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=2 y + 2$ from $(6,2)$ to $(8,3).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2 t + 2.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2 t + 2,\\,t⟩,\\,2\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $2\\le t\\le 3$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t + 2)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=8 y,$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =8 t \\\\  & =8 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}8 y\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\left(8 t\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}8 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}8 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\left[4 \\sqrt{5} t^{2}\\right]_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =8 \\sqrt{5}\\left(\\frac{3^2}{2}-\\frac{2^2}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =8 \\sqrt{5}\\left(\\frac{9}{2}-2\\right) \\\\  & =20 \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ee718e7-8c66-5b5c-9686-158a4a052a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{2} + \\frac{343}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519937} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2f283d-ca77-5bd5-b76f-fd081e1ef092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{343}{2} - \\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519942} {:answer/id #uuid "985323ac-4ffe-5a8b-b35b-a8ae16606764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{343}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519952} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec560c5-8a2a-5832-803c-a59a7a317dea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "891" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519955} {:answer/id #uuid "aa5db845-80f2-5dbc-b2a3-2f9cc3faee50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d2f283d-ca77-5bd5-b76f-fd081e1ef092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{343}{2} - \\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519942} :answer-field/id #uuid "64569d65-6b5b-57eb-a178-6af1a5ac90dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1335390-7338-553c-9752-14a0d9faa957" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca91ec7d1e638b49ab7d4334397c5c7d383b7df0bce022c0e481b857ae2e1b95.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}\\frac{6 x}{y}\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=y^{2}$ from $(1,1)$ to $(12,2 \\sqrt{3}),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=t^{2}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t^{2},\\,t⟩,\\,1\\le t\\le 2 \\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $1\\le t\\le 2 \\sqrt{3}$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2 t\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 t)^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=\\frac{6 x}{y},$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{6 \\left(t^{2}\\right)}{t} \\\\  & =6 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{6 x}{y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}\\left(6 t\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}6 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve this using the substitution $u=4 t^{2} + 1,$ $\\text{d}u=8 t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}6 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & =6{\\int }_{5}^{49}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{49}\\frac{3 \\sqrt{u}}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\right]_{5}^{49} \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{2}\\right]_{5}^{49} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(49\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(5\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{343}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{343}{2} - \\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519969 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d5f72a-c449-56eb-989f-22226e0b50de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519914} {:answer/id #uuid "128d4ac3-24ee-55ce-9b25-4cf80792cec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519916} {:answer/id #uuid "7d024a42-dbb0-595d-9286-4d48315042fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519945} {:answer/id #uuid "a286ac33-a522-5b67-b3fa-62a475c8f733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519959} {:answer/id #uuid "b4231752-2303-5f37-a885-fec04df72753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a286ac33-a522-5b67-b3fa-62a475c8f733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519959} :answer-field/id #uuid "5aabe041-866e-5d3f-b02e-f537a8abdf22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d33ab010-ae47-54a5-a66e-bc5313115fb2" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}6 y\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=2 y + 2$ from $(4,1)$ to $(6,2).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2 t + 2.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2 t + 2,\\,t⟩,\\,1\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $1\\le t\\le 2$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t + 2)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=6 y,$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =6 t \\\\  & =6 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}6 y\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\left(6 t\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}6 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}6 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\left[3 \\sqrt{5} t^{2}\\right]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =6 \\sqrt{5}\\left(\\frac{2^2}{2}-\\frac{1^2}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =6 \\sqrt{5}\\left(2-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =9 \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1baa52c1-5c71-5f87-8551-3279611003dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519919} {:answer/id #uuid "67732790-16a3-5527-b750-580381646c5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519940} {:answer/id #uuid "8e21c30b-33aa-5878-9f58-a724973bf4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "116 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519950} {:answer/id #uuid "9d078917-01b7-5c9d-8b60-6b5248691b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519954} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9d7d72-6508-5e36-8e89-fed8dd873be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "312 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d078917-01b7-5c9d-8b60-6b5248691b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519954} :answer-field/id #uuid "afcc0b52-3f45-5cf3-a53f-e03a34d67289" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "edc5b731-7331-5410-b96a-68df46082b51" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}8 y\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=2 y + 2$ from $(6,2)$ to $(12,5).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2 t + 2.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2 t + 2,\\,t⟩,\\,2\\le t\\le 5\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $2\\le t\\le 5$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t + 2)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=8 y,$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =8 t \\\\  & =8 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}8 y\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\left(8 t\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}8 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}8 \\sqrt{5} t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\left[4 \\sqrt{5} t^{2}\\right]_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =8 \\sqrt{5}\\left(\\frac{5^2}{2}-\\frac{2^2}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =8 \\sqrt{5}\\left(\\frac{25}{2}-2\\right) \\\\  & =84 \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16637d83-9d55-58dd-9a6e-b892dcb60c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{64 \\sqrt{2}}{15} + \\frac{832 \\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519918} {:answer/id #uuid "2aae3009-c21c-529f-9656-63ab4497ccd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{832 \\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519920} {:answer/id #uuid "d57a9be7-b91b-5c57-b613-1fb34ee7dd87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{32}{5} + 160 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519970} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b390e9-d955-54c3-bde9-22bd5a28116c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5120}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519975} {:answer/id #uuid "f5509479-ec88-5363-9bf0-f7d33b99fdee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64 \\sqrt{2}}{15} + \\frac{832 \\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16637d83-9d55-58dd-9a6e-b892dcb60c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{64 \\sqrt{2}}{15} + \\frac{832 \\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519918} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1f6ae96-8b2e-581c-93a9-a1569f0c7cc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f20094c6-0c28-54cf-af5d-3c0a666f7927" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad80637c8c61ee847bd385c39fb0eec5fc1b14ee4f9d6c1796fb31baff48c016.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral\n${\\int }_{C}8 x y\\,\\text{d}s,$\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=2 \\sqrt{y}$ from $(2,1)$ to $(2 \\sqrt{5},5),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y),$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2 \\sqrt{t}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2 \\sqrt{t},\\,t⟩,\\,1\\le t\\le 5\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $1\\le t\\le 5$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 \\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}})^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{t}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{1}{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=8 x y,$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =8 \\left(2 \\sqrt{t}\\right) t \\\\  & =16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}8 x y\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\left(16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{1}{t}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}16 t \\sqrt{t + 1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve this using the substitution $u=4 t + 4,$ $\\text{d}u=4\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}16 t \\sqrt{t + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & =8{\\int }_{8}^{24}\\frac{u-4}{4}\\cdot\\sqrt{u}\\cdot\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{24}\\frac{u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{2} - 2 \\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2}{5}u^{5/2}-(4)\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\right)\\right]_{8}^{24} \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{5} - \\frac{4 u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right]_{8}^{24} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(24\\right)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{5}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{4 \\left(24\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(8\\right)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{5}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{4 \\left(8\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{1152 \\sqrt{6}}{5}\\right)+\\left(- 64 \\sqrt{6}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{128 \\sqrt{2}}{5}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{64 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{64 \\sqrt{2}}{15} + \\frac{832 \\sqrt{6}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520447 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fbcae67-db75-584e-abdf-39bdb2826748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1)=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520011} {:answer/id #uuid "16929637-3274-5e13-ac66-9758de4de287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1)=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520023} {:answer/id #uuid "478dcde0-ffcc-5e5b-9556-15d26a321acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1)=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520099} {:answer/id #uuid "5ed5baec-393d-5e5f-af72-0e15849dbfe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1)=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520138} {:answer/id #uuid "e70f5fff-9528-5097-9f8b-f32c917cacb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1)=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ed5baec-393d-5e5f-af72-0e15849dbfe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1)=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520138} :answer-field/id #uuid "140d3701-ba23-5c26-9cf9-6d695b5d1f47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01c94ce2-04ad-5708-8ba5-8bfca9809325" :question/math-academy-id "q-101950" :question/problem "Find the instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)=5{x}^{2}$ at the point $x=1$ by computing the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "*Method 1:*\n\nBy the definition, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(1)={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(1+h)-f(1)}{h}.\n$$\n\nApplying this to $f(x)=5{x}^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{5(1+h)^{2}-5(1)^{2}}{h}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{5+10h+5{h}^{2}-5}{h}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{10h+5{h}^{2}}{h}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}(10+5h) \\\\  & =10+(0) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n*Method 2:*\n\nBy the definition, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(1)={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{f(x)-f(1)}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nApplying this to $f(x)=5{x}^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}(\\frac{5{x}^{2}-5(1)^{2}}{x-1}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}(\\frac{5({x}^{2}-1)}{x-1}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}(\\frac{5(x-1)(x+1)}{x-1}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}5(x+1) \\\\  & =5(1+1) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b420ea0-e242-5852-9a3b-163544334e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520075} {:answer/id #uuid "4d1c5347-c759-549b-a191-bc31ec802b90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520109} {:answer/id #uuid "dedd649a-149f-5255-a5fc-3c20f9338e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520314} {:answer/id #uuid "e6bfe5a6-d3b1-5081-ab2c-efd0c7a6f4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520328} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc01020-4089-56e6-82f5-6c8e9efb10f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dedd649a-149f-5255-a5fc-3c20f9338e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520314} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec37af3f-2077-53c3-aed3-459ba8fcb5e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13aa670b-3e27-50cc-b24b-f562a4443719" :question/math-academy-id "q-146337" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(x+{y}^{2})}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x+1}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3x+{y}^{2}}{8})}{(\\frac{3x+1}{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(x+{y}^{2})}{3x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{3\\cdot 1+1}=\\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+{y}^{3})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49e3ff31-b227-5b2a-8fe3-d34a74248ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520103} {:answer/id #uuid "8262ba09-25dc-5226-a050-4bcaa05979b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+y}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520182} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ece17e-ce07-5a63-9272-3986c9fc0b28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520253} {:answer/id #uuid "da064ca0-ec2d-5668-b781-affcc343f33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+y}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520299} {:answer/id #uuid "fa62812a-5ad0-5c54-8abe-7a6dfef958dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23x}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa62812a-5ad0-5c54-8abe-7a6dfef958dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23x}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520358} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f740bd4-a687-5983-91a3-7513fe971934" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "200b9c27-2539-5e86-b17a-fa5314a06310" :question/math-academy-id "q-146517" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6(x+y)}{5}, & x\\le y\\le 2x,\\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6(x+y)}{5})}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+y)}{5{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\le y\\le 2x,\\,0<x<1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{x}^{2x}y\\cdot \\,\\frac{2(x+y)}{5{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{x}^{2x}(xy+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}}{[\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{x}^{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}}[(\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3})-(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{23{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{23x\\cdot \\cancel{({x}^{2})}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{23x}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520464 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ccc6750-246a-5a6e-8d0b-5e04b2fcec20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+2y)}{4(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520032} {:answer/id #uuid "445f339a-c1d1-5908-9ed9-b51956b4aff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(1+2y)}{4(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520089} {:answer/id #uuid "73ea5849-0a8b-5581-9a68-493551edf6c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+2y)}{(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520159} {:answer/id #uuid "8bf1aa4b-de93-56ed-90a9-5e53ffe6181a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{2(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520196} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a557fd-77df-511c-836c-c00052e9bf42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{4(y+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "445f339a-c1d1-5908-9ed9-b51956b4aff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(1+2y)}{4(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520089} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5798b6-1edf-5ed2-bbb7-aae35b6bf653" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c1f6156-411f-54e4-bb68-bbf84af25120" :question/math-academy-id "q-146520" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{5}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y+2}{5}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0<y<1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{5})}{(\\frac{6y+2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{6y+2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\,\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{6y+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6y+2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+xy)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6y+2}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6y+2}[\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{y}{2}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6y+2}\\cdot \\frac{1+2y}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2(3y+1)}\\cdot \\frac{(1+2y)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1+2y)}{4(3y+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520466 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf9c026-9fde-556b-a693-fbda3046a227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+4y)}{(1+3y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520030} {:answer/id #uuid "46d79442-5892-5af0-818d-d2ead962340e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(y+3)}{3(y+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520098} {:answer/id #uuid "5345dbd5-7e99-5317-8490-c789146a8788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+3y)}{(1+4y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520116} {:answer/id #uuid "db470a65-0a51-550a-8ffd-cf65f10f85a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+3y)}{3(1+4y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520305} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e56427-f6a7-5af0-99d9-80933b07e001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+3y)}{3(1+4y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db470a65-0a51-550a-8ffd-cf65f10f85a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+3y)}{3(1+4y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520305} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1a039c4-3510-5a92-9df7-feb0d8d5d857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5142c769-0ab4-5c62-90f2-d5f937ec0c66" :question/math-academy-id "q-146538" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(x+2y)}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+4y}{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2(x+2y)}{3})}{(\\frac{1+4y}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+2y)}{1+4y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\,\\frac{2(x+2y)}{1+4y}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+4y}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+2yx)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+4y}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+y{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+4y}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}+y-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+4y}\\cdot \\frac{1+3y}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1+3y)}{3(1+4y)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14e307ca-013b-55ec-82b5-1e7ce273b025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520019} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdd1b05-efac-5cd2-b80d-adb096167f01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520173} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba03e74-688b-57d5-9691-01500fb67606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520210} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f36e7e-f5c6-5149-a6a3-fc6ab2a6b267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520349} {:answer/id #uuid "f756e2bb-9a31-56ee-859f-f341ea8ca2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f756e2bb-9a31-56ee-859f-f341ea8ca2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520352} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd6a3276-afa5-552e-8370-0df3289262b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56f1a503-7979-5afa-a86c-36de0338e547" :question/math-academy-id "q-95522" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{(5x)\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}})\\cdot (5x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520474 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b7b8be0-cd7d-5f2a-8d07-58b09b3e02bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520106} {:answer/id #uuid "51d6868e-9f63-566b-8657-3e46a79dcf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520115} {:answer/id #uuid "a358ba73-65d0-5ebe-ae65-bacd7eb25e86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520216} {:answer/id #uuid "a6fae95c-8607-5baf-bcfe-438d0e382039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520220} {:answer/id #uuid "cf07accb-49d6-5bf1-b6e5-cfad1ed38be2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51d6868e-9f63-566b-8657-3e46a79dcf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520115} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a063c31-7ea1-511c-9093-dca00ca75be6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7abac60c-426c-5228-9bff-bdb217864577" :question/math-academy-id "q-146397" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{4})}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0<x<1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\cdot \\,\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}[4-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520482 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12cc6b99-6aa4-5495-b69d-7c177d70318b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3(2)^{2}}{x-2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520015} {:answer/id #uuid "2ef965a1-569c-55ee-955d-a534fc912f4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3(2)^{2}}{{x}^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520061} {:answer/id #uuid "4b9b3af5-c3c8-599f-a61a-22160b2775b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3(2)^{2}}{x-2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520107} {:answer/id #uuid "896cf965-91e5-5f59-949b-28482f31bce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3(2)^{2}}{x+2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520194} {:answer/id #uuid "dddc1051-6963-51f0-a801-9b25da83d366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3(2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b9b3af5-c3c8-599f-a61a-22160b2775b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3(2)^{2}}{x-2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520107} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fdf64b2-7dfc-5534-bdd0-a30466c74ca2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "864d30c1-9b9e-5747-9ebf-06a4c172035c" :question/math-academy-id "q-47870" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=3{x}^{2}$, what is ${f}^{′}(2)$ according to the definition?" :question/worked-solution "The definition of ${f}^{′}(2)$ is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{f(x)-f(a)}{x-a}).\n$$\n\nLet $a=2.$ Then, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}-3(2)^{2}}{x-2}).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520483 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2645204e-4a2f-5bad-beb3-763d90807c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520046} {:answer/id #uuid "294f333b-a9d4-562a-8eae-492cfcc89909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520049} {:answer/id #uuid "536f3405-9be4-55d8-a59a-c53890d35b59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520118} {:answer/id #uuid "66bb441d-dd19-59af-b152-79149e4a3104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520146} {:answer/id #uuid "c82d5f0d-b3be-5af8-87e6-5da9ad05a797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "294f333b-a9d4-562a-8eae-492cfcc89909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520049} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6245f27-68e2-534e-b326-9a13a0b95dff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ddac48b-cef1-5d70-9862-741511be4eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-125855" :question/problem "$$\n\n$\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{15}{17})=$" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{15}{17}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+(-\\frac{15}{17})}{1-(-\\frac{15}{17})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-\\frac{15}{17}}{1+\\frac{15}{17}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{2}{15}}{\\frac{32}{15}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{-4} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cca56e0-bd46-5cdc-92e5-fbf4d373740e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520059} {:answer/id #uuid "4ac055dd-9f86-515e-b1ae-23330cb8d42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520104} {:answer/id #uuid "5f33329f-ed6e-55fc-8a52-3418bf264493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520139} {:answer/id #uuid "728d87fa-4ae9-5abf-a254-4e2127b85d13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520156} {:answer/id #uuid "72957adc-bbda-5a70-8bcf-de083ff0510a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72957adc-bbda-5a70-8bcf-de083ff0510a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520157} :answer-field/id #uuid "08605099-e0ee-5781-8ffd-d1bea3536f65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9750db93-431a-52f4-a35e-36e894133bed" :question/math-academy-id "q-125859" :question/problem "$$\n\nGiven that $t>-\\frac{1}{2},$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{t}{t+1})?$" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{t}{t+1}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+\\frac{t}{t+1}}{1-\\frac{t}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{t+1+t}{t+1}}{\\frac{t+1-t}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{2t+1}{t+1}}{\\frac{1}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6fd54d-4c1c-55c6-8760-81621dbc6cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520007} {:answer/id #uuid "1ddc283e-0948-540b-b84c-d2835daf8f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520035} {:answer/id #uuid "416e4a5c-22d6-5be2-bec7-c3eae49ba017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520084} {:answer/id #uuid "4661b057-e34b-5ad1-86ad-f2170ff87ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520095} {:answer/id #uuid "ef193c69-7a43-5081-98b8-a77c6b8cc73b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4661b057-e34b-5ad1-86ad-f2170ff87ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520095} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce1f1101-3df3-5c9e-9c08-818c39307178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b25c780b-4145-5bfa-8e04-0856e9d67d3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-146253" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3y}{12}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+1}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2x+3y}{12})}{(\\frac{y+1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+3y}{3y+3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{2x+3\\cdot 1}{3\\cdot 1+3}=\\frac{2x+3}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{2x+3}{6}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(2{x}^{2}+3x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}((\\frac{16}{3}+6)-(\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{3}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{55}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3f5e67e-74f8-5482-8c10-428bbd5c2446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1+4x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3f5e67e-74f8-5482-8c10-428bbd5c2446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1+4x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520289} :answer-field/id #uuid "64aa8422-e168-5f7f-b4b2-8eebac1df31f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8788c2a-c953-5587-a4b0-071fdea7bf08" :question/math-academy-id "q-313233" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(2x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{|x|}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(3\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|2x|\\sqrt{1+(2x)^{2}}})\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2|x|\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|x|}\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213c31e4-604c-5637-a050-4eaeb6c0f751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520038} {:answer/id #uuid "878b145b-533e-56a3-a50a-7a45a1f3deec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520191} {:answer/id #uuid "b5cff024-e8a3-5830-b01f-71c191133afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520247} {:answer/id #uuid "b6db8036-e893-58df-8210-1dab0e50bf02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520248} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9dc1c3-ffa1-5373-bb29-a4874096f214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5cff024-e8a3-5830-b01f-71c191133afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520247} :answer-field/id #uuid "57708cab-0a02-5b87-93ec-6746644b7829" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0b66b9d-4d88-5de4-a9f2-e4468c8b8ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163105" :question/problem "For the function of two variables \n$f(x,y)=\\sqrt{x+y+4},$\nthe quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2+ax+\\frac{1}{4}y-\\frac{1}{64}{x}^{2}+bxy+c{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "If the function $f(x,y)$ is twice differentiable at $(x,y)=(0,0),$ then the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈\\overbrace{f(0,0)+{f}_{x}(0,0)\\cdot x+{f}_{y}(0,0)\\cdot y}^{\\text{Linear approximation}} \\\\  & \\,\\,+\\underbrace{\\frac{1}{2}({f}_{xx}(0,0)\\cdot {x}^{2}+2{f}_{xy}(0,0)\\cdot xy+{f}_{yy}(0,0)\\cdot {y}^{2})}_{\\text{Quadratic part}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the terms of our Taylor polynomial.\n\n- Calculating the value of the function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the first derivatives, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y+4}}, & \\,{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y+4}} \\\\ {f}_{x}(0,0) & =\\frac{1}{4}, & \\,{f}_{y}(0,0) & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the second derivatives, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{(x+y+4)^{3}}}, & \\,{f}_{xx}(0,0) & =-\\frac{1}{32} \\\\ {f}_{xy}(x,y) & =-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{(x+y+4)^{3}}}, & \\,{f}_{xy}(0,0) & =-\\frac{1}{32} \\\\ {f}_{yy}(x,y) & =-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{(x+y+4)^{3}}}, & \\,{f}_{yy}(0,0) & =-\\frac{1}{32}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈2+\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot x+\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot y+\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{32}\\cdot {x}^{2}+2(-\\frac{1}{32})\\cdot xy+(-\\frac{1}{32})\\cdot {y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{4}x+\\frac{1}{4}y-\\frac{1}{64}{x}^{2}+(-\\frac{1}{32})xy+(-\\frac{1}{64}){y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na+b+c=\\frac{1}{4}+(-\\frac{1}{32})+(-\\frac{1}{64})=\\frac{13}{64}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33c7c493-bcdb-5703-aa16-7951eec23ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520068} {:answer/id #uuid "961a1fb5-7dbb-4d31-93ea-cbe5abcbdc15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33c7c493-bcdb-5703-aa16-7951eec23ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520068} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b694189-fec1-5a06-8456-a524e215acf6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa666076-05a3-50c7-be3d-b7a39d6d4f55" :question/math-academy-id "q-314192" :question/problem "The slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{4x+1}$ at the point where $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=4x+1.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4x+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4x+1}})|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4(0)+1}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43ad5b43-aace-5d3d-a358-724cb263373e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2688}{5} - \\frac{784384 \\sqrt{2}}{945}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520675} {:answer/id #uuid "488a74d3-7dcc-59c5-a18f-dfc26f0e4a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 - \\frac{128 \\sqrt{2}}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520676} {:answer/id #uuid "ba09aabf-f5f1-5b41-8fdb-b6dacd6f5500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520707} {:answer/id #uuid "dac02ed1-55d3-5134-9bb8-1308a80f0326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{8704 \\sqrt{2}}{105}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520720} {:answer/id #uuid "e19d4737-fdde-54f7-b02d-3480dff1be65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 - \\frac{8704 \\sqrt{2}}{105}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19d4737-fdde-54f7-b02d-3480dff1be65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 - \\frac{8704 \\sqrt{2}}{105}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520723} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1997853-2be2-51a6-9186-222b0926a788" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "145cd2cc-e119-5363-8df0-50511cd77f67" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=- x - 3 y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3},\\,2 t^{2} - 4 t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3},\\,2 t^{2} - 4 t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}$ and $y=2 t^{2} - 4 t.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t^{2} - 4 t)j \\\\ &=(8 \\sqrt{t})i+(4 t - 4)j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(8 \\sqrt{t})^2+(4 t - 4)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{64t+16(t-1)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{16(t^2+2t+1)} \\\\ &=4|t+1| \\\\ &=4 t + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t+1|=t+1$ since $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=- x - 3 y$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(-1)(\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3})+(-3)(2 t^{2} - 4 t) \\\\ &=- \\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} - 6 t^{2} + 12 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C - x - 3 y\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2}(- \\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} - 6 t^{2} + 12 t)\\cdot (4 t + 4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2}- \\frac{64}{3}t^{3/2}(t+1)+(-48)(t^2/2-t)(t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2}- \\frac{64 t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3} - \\frac{64 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} - 24 t^{3} + 24 t^{2} + 48 t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[(- \\frac{128 t^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21})+(- \\frac{128 t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{15})+(- 6 t^{4})+(8 t^{3})+(24 t^{2})\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left((- \\frac{128 (2)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21})+(- \\frac{128 (2)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{15})+(- 6 (2)^{4})+(8 (2)^{3})+(24 (2)^{2})\\right)-\\left((- \\frac{128 (0)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21})+(- \\frac{128 (0)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{15})+(- 6 (0)^{4})+(8 (0)^{3})+(24 (0)^{2})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((- \\frac{1024 \\sqrt{2}}{21})+(- \\frac{512 \\sqrt{2}}{15})+(-96)+(64)+(96)\\right)-\\left((0)+(0)+(0)+(0)+(0)\\right) \\\\ &=64 - \\frac{8704 \\sqrt{2}}{105}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "400cf204-a287-54da-8cf6-8f6c5520cca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520673} {:answer/id #uuid "a20dac01-182b-507b-bf2f-639fa423045a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "940" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520700} {:answer/id #uuid "aa3bf514-31bd-5be2-b51b-27b23cca2950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{212050}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520703} {:answer/id #uuid "adb18c45-c4c6-5d1a-bc95-d4057d6c1d2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1582}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520704} {:answer/id #uuid "d53c1a86-d5cc-5a33-a7f3-31c1f8e70e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5940" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d53c1a86-d5cc-5a33-a7f3-31c1f8e70e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5940" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520718} :answer-field/id #uuid "67baca2f-3def-5b74-8464-fcb9eed2a55b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2136d6d7-0ed7-55ff-b190-1b731f49a8bb" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} + 2 y^{2} - 3$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩$ for $t\\in [1,3].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ &=(5)(-\\sin t+\\sin t+t\\cos t)i+(5)(\\cos t-\\cos t+t\\sin t)j \\\\ &=(5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+(5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{25t^2(\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t)} \\\\ &=5|t| \\\\ &=5 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} + 2 y^{2} - 3$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(2)\\left((5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2\\right)+(-3) \\\\ &=(50)\\left(\\cos^2t+2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\sin^2t+\\sin^2t-2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\cos^2t\\right)+(-3) \\\\ &=(50)(1+t^2)+(-3) \\\\ &=50 t^{2} + 47\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C 2 x^{2} + 2 y^{2} - 3\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{1}^{3}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{3}(50 t^{2} + 47)\\cdot (5 t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{3}250 t^{3} + 235 t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[(\\frac{235 t^{2}}{2})+(\\frac{125 t^{4}}{2})\\right]_{1}^{3} \\\\ &=\\left((\\frac{235 (3)^{2}}{2})+(\\frac{125 (3)^{4}}{2})\\right)-\\left((\\frac{235 (1)^{2}}{2})+(\\frac{125 (1)^{4}}{2})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((\\frac{2115}{2})+(\\frac{10125}{2})\\right)-\\left((\\frac{235}{2})+(\\frac{125}{2})\\right) \\\\ &=5940.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4d59fc-515b-5f6a-9dc6-509c6e675345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520665} {:answer/id #uuid "48c82739-041c-56fa-8753-1bfa7fa0ee17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520677} {:answer/id #uuid "5e065b1b-4ec3-533f-9c2b-6e064e094ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520681} {:answer/id #uuid "797a833b-97df-53a4-a250-ba3c8eab7778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520692} {:answer/id #uuid "d047b09d-1678-5550-904c-27b96dd5e577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e065b1b-4ec3-533f-9c2b-6e064e094ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520681} :answer-field/id #uuid "dffa612e-a99a-5518-aa59-ddebaf8c26ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2cfdc280-62d5-528b-8c5c-9974a8b2cb2c" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=2 x + 2 y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨- 2 t,\\,- 2 t - 2⟩$ for $t\\in [-2,0].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨- 2 t,\\,- 2 t - 2⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=- 2 t$ and $y=- 2 t - 2.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t - 2)j \\\\ &=(-2)i+(-2)j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(-2)^2+(-2)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{8} \\\\ &=2 \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=2 x + 2 y$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(2)\\left(- 2 t+(- 2 t - 2)\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 t - 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C 2 x + 2 y\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{-2}^{0}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-2}^{0}(- 8 t - 4)\\cdot (2 \\sqrt{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(2 \\sqrt{2})\\int_{-2}^{0}- 8 t - 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-2}^{0}- 16 \\sqrt{2} t - 8 \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(4 \\sqrt{2})\\left[- 2 t^{2}+(- 2 t)\\right]_{-2}^{0} \\\\ &=\\left[(- 8 \\sqrt{2} t^{2})+(- 8 \\sqrt{2} t)\\right]_{-2}^{0} \\\\ &=\\left((- 8 \\sqrt{2} (0)^{2})+(- 8 \\sqrt{2} (0))\\right)-\\left((- 8 \\sqrt{2} (-2)^{2})+(- 8 \\sqrt{2} (-2))\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((0)+(0)\\right)-\\left((- 32 \\sqrt{2})+(16 \\sqrt{2})\\right) \\\\ &=16 \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520686 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03873494-83c0-5778-9053-50e3cd0a8960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520659} {:answer/id #uuid "067f6b16-2ef2-5fc3-a21a-839c972f0942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2} - \\frac{27 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520661} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2be384-eb81-581d-887c-e86a86517461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520680} {:answer/id #uuid "74ba6b0b-7f7b-585f-8489-1ebb8057a589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{81}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520689} {:answer/id #uuid "c6be7094-4eda-5791-84ae-661427999cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6be7094-4eda-5791-84ae-661427999cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520713} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b93d243-d980-5d5b-a615-915dffb75464" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6b0f1fc6-a816-51a9-b852-0409900ea7be" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=9 - 2 x^{2}$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩$ for $t\\in [- \\frac{\\pi}{2},- \\frac{\\pi}{4}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ &=(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})i+(- 3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(- 3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{9\\sin^2t+9\\cos^2t} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{9(\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t)} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{9} \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=9 - 2 x^{2}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(-1)\\left(2(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2-9\\right) \\\\ &=(-9)(2\\cos^2t-1) \\\\ &=- 9 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C 9 - 2 x^{2}\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}(- 9 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)})\\cdot (3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}- 27 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=-27\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\cos 2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(-27)\\left[\\frac{1}{2}\\sin 2t\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\\\ &=\\left[(- \\frac{27 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2})\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\\\ &=\\left((- \\frac{27 \\sin{\\left(2 (- \\frac{\\pi}{4}) \\right)}}{2})\\right)-\\left((- \\frac{27 \\sin{\\left(2 (- \\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\right)}}{2})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((\\frac{27}{2})\\right)-\\left((0)\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26cafdf9-bb1b-5db6-9f2c-63c617017df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520667} {:answer/id #uuid "3d86a63d-975f-514b-aa2d-6a9a2dda1a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520672} {:answer/id #uuid "649c7469-e587-53cb-ad3a-e1aa2a960ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520682} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6f206b-ea3f-54ac-8df3-223331b388be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520696} {:answer/id #uuid "f6004e5c-0f89-546c-9a29-395a9815c45a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d86a63d-975f-514b-aa2d-6a9a2dda1a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520672} :answer-field/id #uuid "94de007f-b740-55aa-979f-480b58ced30a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d171fb6-8597-5d32-b391-80e23689046f" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=- 2 x - 2 y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨- t,\\,1 - t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨- t,\\,1 - t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=- t$ and $y=1 - t.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1 - t)j \\\\ &=(-1)i+(-1)j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(-1)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=- 2 x - 2 y$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(-2)\\left(- t+(1 - t)\\right) \\\\ &=4 t - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C - 2 x - 2 y\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{3}(4 t - 2)\\cdot (\\sqrt{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(\\sqrt{2})\\int_{0}^{3}4 t - 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{3}4 \\sqrt{2} t - 2 \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(- 2 \\sqrt{2})\\left[- t^{2}+(t)\\right]_{0}^{3} \\\\ &=\\left[(2 \\sqrt{2} t^{2})+(- 2 \\sqrt{2} t)\\right]_{0}^{3} \\\\ &=\\left((2 \\sqrt{2} (3)^{2})+(- 2 \\sqrt{2} (3))\\right)-\\left((2 \\sqrt{2} (0)^{2})+(- 2 \\sqrt{2} (0))\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((18 \\sqrt{2})+(- 6 \\sqrt{2})\\right)-\\left((0)+(0)\\right) \\\\ &=12 \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520693 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48c9bce6-a245-551e-932e-0da2c01469dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{32 \\pi^{3}}{3} - 34 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520678} {:answer/id #uuid "67d2b09b-2ddd-5417-8f12-3e433a7e207d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 68 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520684} {:answer/id #uuid "8600936c-7807-533f-b7ec-6363eb423607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 \\pi^{2} \\left(- \\pi^{2} - 2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520695} {:answer/id #uuid "afcc62a2-a04f-5e40-840e-4035cd3ad69e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^{2} \\left(- 32 \\pi^{2} - 68\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520705} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7f42b2-a1b5-58b8-b1c4-f9b190a7088f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32 \\pi^{3} \\left(- 48 \\pi^{2} - 85\\right)}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afcc62a2-a04f-5e40-840e-4035cd3ad69e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^{2} \\left(- 32 \\pi^{2} - 68\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520705} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3dd3542-87fa-5542-a06b-ffafba3d77a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7c78a6b5-a741-5677-9ee8-db5e516f2ee1" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=- 2 x^{2} - 2 y^{2} - 2$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ &=(4)(-\\sin t+\\sin t+t\\cos t)i+(4)(\\cos t-\\cos t+t\\sin t)j \\\\ &=(4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+(4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{16t^2(\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t)} \\\\ &=4|t| \\\\ &=4 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=- 2 x^{2} - 2 y^{2} - 2$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(-2)\\left((4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2\\right)+(-2) \\\\ &=(-32)\\left(\\cos^2t+2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\sin^2t+\\sin^2t-2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\cos^2t\\right)+(-2) \\\\ &=(-32)(1+t^2)+(-2) \\\\ &=- 32 t^{2} - 34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C - 2 x^{2} - 2 y^{2} - 2\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}(- 32 t^{2} - 34)\\cdot (4 t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}- 128 t^{3} - 136 t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[(- 68 t^{2})+(- 32 t^{4})\\right]_{0}^{\\pi} \\\\ &=\\left((- 68 (\\pi)^{2})+(- 32 (\\pi)^{4})\\right)-\\left((- 68 (0)^{2})+(- 32 (0)^{4})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((- 68 \\pi^{2})+(- 32 \\pi^{4})\\right)-\\left((0)+(0)\\right) \\\\ &=\\pi^{2} \\left(- 32 \\pi^{2} - 68\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520721 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0651e1c4-08b2-560b-bab1-0ee3946b48cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5245}{84} + \\frac{2720 \\sqrt{2}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520660} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9a2970-315f-5d30-bdd2-2c7a3e0457b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 + \\frac{32 \\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520671} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee0d219-cf7d-50b1-a2df-423d51c39b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{160}{7} + \\frac{2720 \\sqrt{2}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520697} {:answer/id #uuid "a5969666-b75b-5e6c-a017-710506b5e7b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{475}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520702} {:answer/id #uuid "c083f817-fabc-53b4-9149-8f9984d36ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{127375}{189} + \\frac{306400 \\sqrt{2}}{189}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0651e1c4-08b2-560b-bab1-0ee3946b48cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5245}{84} + \\frac{2720 \\sqrt{2}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520660} :answer-field/id #uuid "763c684e-1374-5918-a1c0-00fb29101703" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dd9ec35c-d87b-5b5e-8742-da91c43c261f" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x + 2 y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3},\\,\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t⟩$ for $t\\in [1,2].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3},\\,\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t)j \\\\ &=(10 \\sqrt{t})i+(5 t - 5)j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(10 \\sqrt{t})^2+(5 t - 5)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{100t+25(t-1)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{25(t^2+2t+1)} \\\\ &=5|t+1| \\\\ &=5 t + 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t+1|=t+1$ since $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=x + 2 y$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(1)(\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3})+(2)(\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t) \\\\ &=\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} + 5 t^{2} - 10 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C x + 2 y\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{1}^{2}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{2}(\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} + 5 t^{2} - 10 t)\\cdot (5 t + 5)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{100}{3}t^{3/2}(t+1)+(50)(t^2/2-t)(t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{100 t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3} + \\frac{100 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} + 25 t^{3} - 25 t^{2} - 50 t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[(\\frac{200 t^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21})+(\\frac{40 t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3})+(\\frac{25 t^{4}}{4})+(- \\frac{25 t^{3}}{3})+(- 25 t^{2})\\right]_{1}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left((\\frac{200 (2)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21})+(\\frac{40 (2)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3})+(\\frac{25 (2)^{4}}{4})+(- \\frac{25 (2)^{3}}{3})+(- 25 (2)^{2})\\right)-\\left((\\frac{200 (1)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21})+(\\frac{40 (1)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3})+(\\frac{25 (1)^{4}}{4})+(- \\frac{25 (1)^{3}}{3})+(- 25 (1)^{2})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((\\frac{1600 \\sqrt{2}}{21})+(\\frac{160 \\sqrt{2}}{3})+(100)+(- \\frac{200}{3})+(-100)\\right)-\\left((\\frac{200}{21})+(\\frac{40}{3})+(\\frac{25}{4})+(- \\frac{25}{3})+(-25)\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{5245}{84} + \\frac{2720 \\sqrt{2}}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68