}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x^{2} - 5 x y^{2} + 6 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x^{2} - 5 x y^{2} + 6 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(4 x - 5 y^{2})\\,i+(- 10 x y + 12 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3}) & =(4 (\\frac{5}{2}) - 5 (\\frac{1}{3})^{2})\\,i+(- 10 (\\frac{5}{2}) (\\frac{1}{3}) + 12 (\\frac{1}{3}))\\,j \\\\  & =(\\frac{85}{9})\\,i+(- \\frac{13}{3})\\,j \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{85}{9},- \\frac{13}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot ⟨x-(\\frac{5}{2}),\\,y-(\\frac{1}{3})⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\frac{85}{9},- \\frac{13}{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨x - \\frac{5}{2},\\,y - \\frac{1}{3}⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08396be8-551a-56f0-be99-5d1834a0c9d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-20,- \\frac{111}{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{3}{2},\\,y + \\frac{5}{2}⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521676} {:answer/id #uuid "10e86575-f93c-5f64-950f-c7b82d9e1364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- \\frac{111}{2},-20⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{3}{2},\\,y - \\frac{5}{2}⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521678} {:answer/id #uuid "186cfe4b-4dfa-530b-9d0d-dd50f922acde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- \\frac{111}{2},-20⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{3}{2},\\,y + \\frac{5}{2}⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521680} {:answer/id #uuid "1d12fff6-b9f1-57fd-a747-267328625646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math