\\frac{25\\pi}{12}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76780c4b-7c67-5172-a923-404203abac6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523048} {:answer/id #uuid "960e68b7-6cec-5c3c-a30f-2031649d16a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{8\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523054} {:answer/id #uuid "a958f4f8-a66f-5de3-aa01-d9ebb099e2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523062} {:answer/id #uuid "eb798864-0ac9-51b0-9c7f-b01a49eef0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523085} {:answer/id #uuid "ec200bf0-4f46-584b-a692-00c1810a50f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec200bf0-4f46-584b-a692-00c1810a50f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523086} :answer-field/id #uuid "25fc8402-d761-5db0-9a28-00207fa0223e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c0cf3c7-a877-56af-bcc4-84567b0dae9c" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\pi t)-8t,\\,y={e}^{1t},\\,0<t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the value of the parameter $t$ at which the normal line to the curve is horizontal." :question/worked-solution "The normal line is horizontal when the tangent line to the curve is vertical. Therefore, we require ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{t}-8,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=1{e}^{1t}\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{t}-8=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{8})=1{e}^{1\\times (1/8)}=e^{\\frac{1}{8}}\\ne 0,\\,\\,\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed horizontal when $t=\\frac{1}{8}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025a69e7-e144-5e44-be3d-307e07729fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "025a69e7-e144-5e44-be3d-307e07729fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523016} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f620562-bc36-5065-97f2-e05de27b5688" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523056} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7a04206-b140-5d42-bde5-4231171751d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7a04206-b140-5d42-bde5-4231171751d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523067} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3f366e8-f2dc-5583-8eb0-e347df6aa6ab" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f7c0d8c-1437-5316-8794-8415de166fad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi}{8}" :db/i