$\n36\\cos(6t-\\frac{\\pi}{6})=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{7\\pi}{9}, \\frac{17\\pi}{18}, \\frac{10\\pi}{9}, \\frac{23\\pi}{18}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\frac{7\\pi}{9}) & =-24\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\frac{17\\pi}{18}) & =24\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\frac{10\\pi}{9}) & =-24\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\frac{23\\pi}{18}) & =24\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed vertical when $t=\\frac{7\\pi}{9}, \\frac{17\\pi}{18}, \\frac{10\\pi}{9}, \\frac{23\\pi}{18}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ad1ca34-78e2-523d-911c-fa01d5fc3a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ad1ca34-78e2-523d-911c-fa01d5fc3a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523021} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ea9c41f-be24-58d4-9192-6a384e99af4d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523024} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8191e8c4-c9d3-55c5-8230-73422d47d05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8191e8c4-c9d3-55c5-8230-73422d47d05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523053} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc59c592-b979-560e-9f61-df9e6c82b700" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2913b10-d5b8-54ac-8c33-5b35f70e8000" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+8,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-8,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the normal to the curve is vertical. Give exact answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the normal to the curve is vertical at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The normal is vertical if the tangent is horizontal. Therefore, we require ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =-5\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) & =5\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed vertical when $t=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $t=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8fb29d2-3496-55af-83fd-601b30be6313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8fb29d2-3496-55af-83fd-601b30be6313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523082} :answer-field/id #uuid "64162304-9344-5df1-b9e3-4a3a21b55152" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523043} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0dc50dc-6e5f-5e29-b38d-35a18468bf05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math}